  "notes": "{正解|せいかい} combines {正|せい} (correct) + {解|かい} (answer/solution).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {正解|せいかい}を{言|い}う/{出|だ}す (to give the correct answer)\n- {正解|せいかい}する (to answer correctly)\n- {正解|せいかい}{率|りつ} (accuracy rate)\n- {全問|ぜんもん}{正解|せいかい} (all answers correct)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {不正解|ふせいかい} (incorrect answer) - antonym\n- {誤答|ごとう} (wrong answer)\n- {解答|かいとう} (answer, solution)\n- {答|こた}え (answer - general)\n\nUSAGE NOTES:\n- Common in quiz shows, tests, and educational contexts\n- Can also be used metaphorically for decisions and judgments",
